Subject: [PATCH] runtime: hands, body, face and eye tracking for games (cranvr)

The runtime offers XR_EXT_hand_tracking, XR_FB_body_tracking,
XR_META_body_tracking_full_body, XR_FB_face_tracking2 and
XR_EXT_eye_gaze_interaction, each while the connected headset offers its
feature. cranvr-host writes the features as words to tracking-features.txt next
to the control file. The runtime reads it when a game lists its instance
extensions, which happens before the control session exists. Without the file
the list is the one of the runtime without the patch.

New control messages: TRACKING_REQUEST (19, runtime to host: the features that
the game uses), HAND_TRACKING (20), BODY_TRACKING (21), FACE_TRACKING (22) and
EYE_GAZE (23). The runtime writes the word "tracking" to runtime-features.txt.
cranvr-host sends 20 to 23 only to a runtime that wrote it. The protocol keeps
its version 9.

A hand and a body arrive as a root pose with velocities and joints in the
headset's tracking space. The runtime moves them into LOCAL like the head and
the controllers and moves them forward by their velocity from the sample's
arrival to the game's locate time, at most 50 ms. xrGetBodySkeletonFB returns a
T-pose skeleton. XR_EXT_eye_gaze_interaction is an interaction profile: an
action on /user/eyes_ext/input/gaze_ext/pose is active while the gaze is
tracked, and xrLocateSpace chains XrEyeGazeSampleTimeEXT.

tests/tracking_smoke.cpp reads every feature through the OpenXR loader and
compares it with the script of cranvr-probe (scripts/e2e.sh --tracking-wine).
---
